## Conventions
- English everywhere (code, comments, logs, docs, commits, PRs). Player text through i18n, en + fr.
- Conventional Commits (`fix(<area>): ...`). Branches `<type>/<issue>-<slug>`.
- One PR per issue, `Closes #n`, body: What / Why / How it was tested / Risk & revert.
- Decisions a future reader would question go in an ADR (`docs/adr/`).

## Hard rules
- No secrets in the repo; placeholders only.
- Never merge, tag, release, or push to the default branch; open PRs.
- Do not replace the owner's libraries (Nexus_*) with third-party ones.
- `needs-decision` issues belong to the maintainer: ask, do not choose.
- Unfixed security weaknesses: neutral issue/PR wording, no exploit details.
- The same manual action twice: propose a skill in `Arffornia/agent-kit`.

